<div class="bhd-page__keypoints" aria-label="Humanitarian hydration principles"><div><strong>Safe water comes first</strong><span>Any powdered hydration product depends on safe preparation water and hygienic handling.</span></div><div><strong>Use the right ORS</strong><span>Diarrhoeal dehydration requires appropriately formulated oral rehydration solution and clinical escalation when severe.</span></div><div><strong>Design for the system</strong><span>Cost, packaging, climate, supply chain, local training and waste all affect whether an intervention works at scale.</span></div></div>

<section class="bhd-page__feature"><div><p class="bhd-page__kicker">ORS for a brighter tomorrow</p><h2>The humanitarian ambition begins with the right solution for the right problem</h2><p>Oral rehydration therapy is one of the most important tools for preventing deaths from diarrhoeal dehydration. WHO reduced-osmolarity ORS is a defined therapeutic formulation, and community access to appropriately prepared ORS is essential during cholera and diarrhoeal outbreaks.</p><p>When Best Hydrate uses the phrase “ORS for a brighter tomorrow,” ORS should mean appropriately formulated and authorized oral rehydration salts in the humanitarian context. It should not imply that the current Best Hydrate consumer product is already equivalent to WHO therapeutic ORS.</p></div></section>

<section class="bhd-page__prose-grid"><article class="bhd-page__prose"><p class="bhd-page__kicker">Field pilot · Botswana · May 2026</p><h2>A small first step from humanitarian intent to field delivery</h2><p>In May 2026, Best Hydrate completed a small community distribution pilot in Botswana, coordinated locally by Oratile in Gaborone and the Goodhope area. A limited amount of Best Hydrate hydration product, together with printed preparation and use guidance, was delivered to community recipients.</p><p>With consent from the local coordinator and photographed recipients, the pilot was documented through field photos and video. The experience provided practical learning around local coordination, transport, clear preparation instructions, respectful documentation and last-mile delivery.</p><p><strong>This was not a clinical study and no treatment or health outcomes were measured.</strong> It was a real-world first step toward learning how future Best Hydrate community and humanitarian hydration initiatives can be delivered responsibly.</p><p><em>Thank you to Oratile for helping coordinate Best Hydrate's first Botswana field-learning effort.</em></p></article><aside class="bhd-page__callout"><span class="bhd-page__callout-label">Field principle</span><h3>Start small. Learn locally. Build responsibly.</h3><p>Future humanitarian programs should grow from real field learning, appropriate formulation, local partnership and transparent evidence.</p></aside></section>

<section class="bhd-page__split"><div class="bhd-page__split-media"><img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/32154745/pexels-photo-32154745.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1500" alt="Community members collecting water from a shared village faucet" width="1500" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><div class="bhd-page__split-copy"><p class="bhd-page__kicker">WASH first</p><h2>A powder cannot solve unsafe water</h2><p>WHO and UNICEF place safe drinking water, sanitation and hygiene at the centre of diarrhoeal disease prevention and emergency response. A powdered oral hydration product only works safely when it can be mixed at the correct concentration with safe water and handled in a way that avoids contamination.</p><p>Humanitarian hydration therefore has to connect product design with WASH, health services, community education and supply systems rather than treating hydration as a stand-alone retail transaction.</p></div></section>

<section class="bhd-page__cards-section"><p class="bhd-page__kicker">Design for deployment</p><h2>Five questions before a humanitarian product leaves the warehouse</h2><div class="bhd-page__cards bhd-page__cards--4"><article><h3>Is the water safe?</h3><p>Preparation instructions are only meaningful if safe water is reliably available.</p></article><article><h3>Is the formulation appropriate?</h3><p>Therapeutic ORS requires the correct composition, authorization and evidence for the intended clinical use.</p></article><article><h3>Can people prepare it correctly?</h3><p>Serving size, language, literacy, measuring tools and package design affect real-world accuracy.</p></article><article><h3>Can supply be sustained?</h3><p>Procurement, storage, transport, shelf stability, local partners and replenishment all shape impact.</p></article></div></section>

<section class="bhd-page__prose-grid"><article class="bhd-page__prose"><p class="bhd-page__kicker">Eco-humanitarian design</p><h2>Lower waste without compromising safety or correct preparation</h2><p>Environmental goals matter in humanitarian logistics because packaging weight, volume and waste scale with distribution. But packaging reductions cannot come at the cost of moisture protection, stability, dosing accuracy, tamper evidence or understandable instructions.</p><p>Best Hydrate's eco-humanitarian work should measure both sides of that equation: material and transport efficiency alongside product integrity and correct use in the target environment.</p></article><aside class="bhd-page__callout"><span class="bhd-page__callout-label">Systems principle</span><h3>Impact = product × access × correct use.</h3><p>A technically good formulation has little value if the water is unsafe, instructions fail or supply disappears.</p></aside></section>

<section class="bhd-page__cards-section"><p class="bhd-page__kicker">Partnership model</p><h2>Build with communities and technical partners</h2><div class="bhd-page__cards bhd-page__cards--3"><article><h3>Local implementation</h3><p>Partners understand language, distribution, community trust and operating constraints that cannot be designed from a distant office.</p></article><article><h3>Research and evaluation</h3><p>Pilots should predefine safety, preparation accuracy, acceptability, access, waste and relevant health or implementation outcomes.</p><a href="/pages/research-impact">Research Impact →</a></article><article><h3>Humanitarian partnerships</h3><p>Use partnerships to connect formulation, procurement, WASH, training and delivery rather than simply donating product.</p><a href="/pages/humanitarian-partnerships">Humanitarian Partnerships →</a></article></div></section>

<section class="bhd-page__brand-context"><div><p class="bhd-page__kicker">Humanitarian standard</p><h2>Do the useful thing, then prove it works in the field</h2><p>Best Hydrate's humanitarian program should earn trust through correct formulation, practical deployment, local collaboration and transparent evidence.</p></div><div class="bhd-page__brand-actions"><a class="bhd-page__button" href="/pages/research-impact">Research Impact</a><a class="bhd-page__button bhd-page__button--secondary" href="/pages/humanitarian-partnerships">Connect With Us</a></div></section>

